From 110b9ab307cca1aae6eeca045865cef4f6d1a144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:50:25 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zed: the About window names Zeo's version

The About window read "Zeo 1.25.0" and "Version 1.25.0+zeo": the product name
came from display_name(), which 0021 makes return "Zeo", but both versions were
Zed's -- CARGO_PKG_VERSION in the heading, AppVersion in the row. Zeo has a
version of its own since 2026-10-05 (zeo/docs/RELEASING.md), and the package
already hands it to the build: src_compile exports RELEASE_VERSION=${PV}, which
until now only `zeo --version` read.

Under the Zeo channel, with RELEASE_VERSION set, the window now reads:

    Zeo 0.2.1                  the heading: Zeo's X.Y.Z, the part before `_p`
    Version  0.2.1_p20261008   the package version, snapshot date included
    Zed      1.25.0+zeo        AppVersion, unchanged

AppVersion is shown, not replaced, because it is what extensions check their
compatibility against; RELEASING.md said so as the reason the About kept Zed's
version, and moving Zed's version to a row of its own keeps that reason intact.
"Copy" carries the same three lines. Without RELEASE_VERSION -- a development
build, or any channel but Zeo -- the window is exactly upstream's.

A separate patch rather than part of 0021 or 0025: neither is about versions,
and this one reads an environment variable only the ebuild sets, which is worth
being able to find by its own name.

(0.2.3_p20261009): the version choice is `package_version_for` and `short_version`, out of
the About window's body so they can be tested.
---

diff --git a/crates/zed/src/zed.rs b/crates/zed/src/zed.rs
index 50959aa..5895d64 100644
--- a/crates/zed/src/zed.rs
+++ b/crates/zed/src/zed.rs
@@ -1525,7 +1525,31 @@ fn initialize_pane(
     });
 }
 
+/// Zeo's own version, as the package passes it in RELEASE_VERSION (`0.2.1_p20261008`);
+/// `None` when it is unset or empty -- a development build -- or on another channel.
+fn package_version_for(
+    release_version: Option<&'static str>,
+    release_channel: ReleaseChannel,
+) -> Option<&'static str> {
+    release_version
+        .filter(|version| !version.is_empty() && release_channel == ReleaseChannel::Zeo)
+}
+
+/// The `X.Y.Z` the About window's title line shows for a package version: the part
+/// before the snapshot suffix (`0.2.1_p20261008` -> `0.2.1`).
+fn short_version(package_version: &str) -> &str {
+    package_version
+        .split('_')
+        .next()
+        .unwrap_or(package_version)
+}
+
 fn open_about_window(cx: &mut App) {
+    /// Zeo's own version, which the package passes in as RELEASE_VERSION.
+    fn zeo_package_version(release_channel: ReleaseChannel) -> Option<&'static str> {
+        package_version_for(option_env!("RELEASE_VERSION"), release_channel)
+    }
+
